Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:04.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Reinforcement learning agents still learn far less efficiently than humans,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.63,0:00:08.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}who freely borrow strategies from many sources and rearrange them at will.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.76,0:00:12.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This work, presented at NeurIPS 2023,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.89,0:00:16.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}introduces Knowledge-Grounded Reinforcement Learning,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.02,0:00:21.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a paradigm that fuses multiple external knowledge policies,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.15,0:00:25.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and a new actor architecture called the Knowledge-Inclusive Attention Network,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.28,0:00:29.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}or KIAN.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.41,0:00:33.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}KIAN lets an agent add, remove, and recombine knowledge policies without retraining,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.54,0:00:37.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and fixes an exploration pathology called entropy imbalance,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.67,0:00:41.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}delivering more sample-efficient and flexible learning across grid-world and robotics tasks.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.10,0:00:46.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Reinforcement learning has succeeded across physics and robotics,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.24,0:00:52.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}yet agents still need enormous numbers of samples to solve tasks that humans master quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.09,0:00:57.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Part of the gap is that humans learn by observing others and freely reuse, combine,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.37,0:00:59.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and swap the strategies they already know.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.04,0:01:06.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Earlier reinforcement learning methods did incorporate external knowledge policies to improve efficiency,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.73,0:01:12.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}but they made it hard to perform arbitrary combinations and replacements of those policies.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.52,0:01:16.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}That rigidity is exactly the property this paper set out to fix.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.89,0:01:19.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The authors summarize five properties of efficient,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.05,0:01:25.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}flexible human learning: being knowledge-acquirable, sample-efficient, generalizable,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.32,0:01:27.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}compositional, and incremental.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.25,0:01:33.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Existing knowledge-guided reinforcement learning methods satisfy some of these but stumble on flexibility.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.82,0:01:38.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}When their fusion mechanism depends on the number or ordering of external policies,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.97,0:01:44.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}rearranging the knowledge set or swapping one policy for another means rebuilding or retraining
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.86,0:01:46.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}large parts of the model.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.41,0:01:52.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The motivation here is to design an actor whose structure lets knowledge policies be freely rearranged,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.80,0:01:57.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}added, or replaced, so a single trained agent can carry its skills into new tasks.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.18,0:02:01.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The paper makes three main contributions.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.94,0:02:05.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}First, it defines Knowledge-Grounded Reinforcement Learning,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.71,0:02:09.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a paradigm that fuses an inner,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.47,0:02:13.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}self-learned policy with multiple external knowledge policies.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.24,0:02:16.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Second, it introduces the Knowledge-Inclusive Attention Network, KIAN,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.00,0:02:20.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}whose embedding-based attention lets knowledge policies be freely rearranged, added,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.76,0:02:24.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}or replaced without touching the rest of the network.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.53,0:02:28.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Third,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.29,0:02:31.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}it uncovers a problem called entropy imbalance that arises when maximizing entropy for exploration,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.06,0:02:35.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}proves when it happens, and proposes modified policy distributions that fix it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.82,0:02:39.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Together these give an agent that is efficient, generalizable,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.59,0:02:43.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and truly modular in its use of knowledge.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.65,0:02:48.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}KIAN, the Knowledge-Inclusive Attention Network, is built from three components.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.83,0:02:54.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The inner actor is a normal learnable policy that lets the agent develop its own strategy,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.66,0:03:00.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so even if every external policy is useless for a task the agent can still find a solution.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.56,0:03:03.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Each knowledge policy, including the inner one,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.60,0:03:06.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}is given a learnable embedding vector called its key,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.04,0:03:11.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}which represents the whole policy independent of any state or action.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.51,0:03:17.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A state-dependent query then produces a vector that is compared to every key by a dot product,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.60,0:03:21.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and a softmax turns those scores into attention weights.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.23,0:03:26.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The agent fuses all policies as a weighted sum and samples the final action.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.15,0:03:31.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Because each key is independent, the policies are unordered, can be rearranged,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.27,0:03:34.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and any one can be replaced just by replacing its key,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.77,0:03:37.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}without retraining the rest of KIAN.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.40,0:03:41.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The experiments span two families of environments.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.30,0:03:45.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}MiniGrid provides discrete-action grid-world tasks of increasing difficulty,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.20,0:03:49.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}from empty rooms to door-key puzzles, dynamic obstacles, lava crossings,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.10,0:03:52.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}multi-room mazes, and key corridors.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.00,0:03:56.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}OpenAI-Robotics provides continuous-control manipulation tasks such as Push, Slide,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.90,0:04:00.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Pick-and-Place, and Reach.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.81,0:04:04.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Crucially,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.71,0:04:08.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}every method starts from the same initial knowledge set built from simple if-else programs
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.61,0:04:12.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}that are deliberately sub-optimal and cannot complete any task on their own.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.51,0:04:16.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Each experiment is repeated with ten random seeds,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.41,0:04:20.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and the reported learning curves show ninety-five percent confidence intervals.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.61,0:04:22.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Across both benchmark suites,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.64,0:04:30.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}KIAN was the only method to succeed in every environment when starting from sub-optimal external knowledge,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.13,0:04:34.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and its sample-efficiency advantage grew as tasks became more complex.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.03,0:04:36.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}In zero-shot generalization,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.99,0:04:41.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}where a policy trained on one task is tested on a different one,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.47,0:04:47.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}KIAN outperformed all baselines in most transfers and did so with noticeably smaller variance.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.06,0:04:50.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On the hardest simple-to-complex grid task,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.07,0:04:56.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}KIAN reached a reward of about 0.93 while the strongest baseline stalled near 0.53.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.88,0:05:02.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}In continuous control, competing methods that ignore the exploration issue collapse,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.76,0:05:05.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}whereas KIAN keeps learning efficiently.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.86,0:05:09.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A key ablation isolates the paper's fix for entropy imbalance.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.05,0:05:13.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}When KIAN runs with the original policy fusion,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.23,0:05:19.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}an agent maximizing entropy for exploration collapses onto a single policy and struggles,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.26,0:05:23.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}especially on demanding tasks like dynamic obstacles, multi-room mazes,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.06,0:05:26.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and the robotic manipulation tasks.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.43,0:05:33.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Switching on the modified policy distributions restores efficient exploration and recovers strong performance.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.87,0:05:39.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Separate compositional and incremental experiments confirm the modular design pays off:
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.76,0:05:45.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}KIAN reuses its learned keys and inner policy to acquire new tasks sequentially with fewer
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.85,0:05:48.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}samples than training each task from scratch.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.19,0:05:51.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A few numbers capture the gains.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.62,0:05:56.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}In zero-shot simple-to-complex transfer on the Empty-Random grid,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.57,0:06:04.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}KIAN scored about 0.93 at the sixteen-by-sixteen size while the best competing method reached only 0.53.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.48,0:06:09.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On the Pick-and-Place task tested at a ten-times-larger goal range,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.57,0:06:13.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}KIAN reached 0.72 against 0.30 for the strongest baseline.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.98,0:06:19.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}In complex-to-simple transfer from DoorKey eight-by-eight to Reach,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.08,0:06:25.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}KIAN achieved a perfect 1.0 versus 0.80 for the reinforcement-learning baselines.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.24,0:06:30.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}All of this is measured across two benchmark suites, five baselines,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.41,0:06:35.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and ten random seeds with ninety-five percent confidence intervals,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.51,0:06:39.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and KIAN is the only method that succeeds everywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.84,0:06:44.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The lasting message is that treating each knowledge policy as an independent,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.72,0:06:50.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}attention-addressable key turns external knowledge into truly modular building blocks.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.16,0:06:51.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}An agent can add, drop,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.62,0:06:55.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}or reorder its policies at any time without retraining the network,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.86,0:07:02.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and the paper's fix for entropy imbalance keeps exploration efficient when many policies are fused.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.13,0:07:07.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The result is a reinforcement learning actor that learns faster, generalizes better,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.45,0:07:08.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and stays flexible,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.65,0:07:13.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}moving agents a step closer to the efficiency and adaptability of human learning.
